# Source-upload filter for `gcloud run deploy --source .` (the trend-trawler-api
# backend image). IMPORTANT: pyproject.toml + uv.lock MUST be uploaded — the root
# Dockerfile COPYs them for `uv sync`. Everything the Python image does not need is
# excluded to keep the upload lean (the .dockerignore further trims the build context).
# Root-only dirs use a leading `/` (gitignore semantics: `bandit/` would also drop
# deployment/bandit/, which runserver/experiments_deploy.py imports).
.git
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env*
.vscode/
.github/
.claude/
.agents/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
a_stash/*
output/*
outputs/
.adk
**/.adk/
frontend/
node_modules/
tests/
docs/
/experiments/
/notebook-examples/
/imgs/
/*.md
# Not imported by the api (runserver never imports bandit/; the traffic job and
# CPR model have their own builds, the Cloud Functions their own deploys).
/bandit/
/bandit_serving/
/bandit_traffic/
/cloud_functions/
